    <item>
      <title>7.1. Closures with parameters</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/7.-closures/7.1.-closures-with-parameters/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/7.-closures/7.1.-closures-with-parameters/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;71-closures-with-parameters&#34;&gt;7.1. Closures with parameters&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#71-closures-with-parameters&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We can take the help of &lt;code&gt;in&lt;/code&gt; keyword to pass parameters in a closure. For example, in the following code, we define a closure to take a person&amp;rsquo;s name as a parameter and say hello to them:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; sayHelloTo = { (name:String) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Hello &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;\(&lt;/span&gt;name&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//calling closure with parameter...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sayHelloTo(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Donald&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It prints:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Hello Donald!&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Do you find a difference between functions and closure in handling the parameter labels? :wink:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>7.2. Closures that return a value</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/7.-closures/7.2.-closures-that-return-a-value/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/7.-closures/7.2.-closures-that-return-a-value/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;72-closures-that-return-a-value&#34;&gt;7.2. Closures that return a value&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#72-closures-that-return-a-value&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To return a value, we would use &lt;code&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; followed by the return data type followed by &lt;code&gt;in&lt;/code&gt; keyword. For example, let&amp;rsquo;s convert the &lt;code&gt;sumOf&lt;/code&gt; function into a closure to return the sum of integers in an array.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; sumOfArray = {(array:[Int]) -&amp;gt; Int &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; sum = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; item &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; array{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        sum &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; item&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//returns the value...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; sum&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//calling the closure with an integer array&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; sum = sumOfArray([&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;])&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;print(sum)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It prints:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>7.3. Closures as parameters</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/7.-closures/7.3.-closures-as-parameters/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/7.-closures/7.3.-closures-as-parameters/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;73-closures-as-parameters&#34;&gt;7.3. Closures as parameters&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#73-closures-as-parameters&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So far, we rewrote the functions as closures. So why write a closure when we can just define a function? Well, the beauty of closures is we can pass closures as parameters to a function. And iOS UIKit and SwiftUI libraries use it extensively.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s define two closures, one to fly and another to drive.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; drive = {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;I am driving!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; fly = {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;I am taking a flight!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now let&amp;rsquo;s recreate a previous scenario where the user could travel from one place to another. So we can write the function as:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
